    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by the high-upside potential of **Christian Yelich** (73.63), who benefits from a favorable matchup against Singer and a strong dynamic platoon edge. While **Christian Yelich** leads the team in projected efficiency, **Junior Caminero** (66.33) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) provide excellent support. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.88) remains a high-leverage start; despite the daunting challenge of facing Skenes, his elite sprint speed and favorable wind conditions at the park provide a unique SB-floor that aligns with our organizational priority on stolen bases, even when the underlying pitching matchup is difficult.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just shy of the 40.0 floor at 39.88. While his contact profile is stable, the combination of a sub-optimal batting order position and negative park adjustments against Leahy suppressed his score, making him a clear bench candidate compared to the deeper utility value of **Kazuma Okamoto** (57.47). We continue to monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Yordan Alvarez** and **Gary Sanchez** are currently unavailable for today\u2019s action. We are also keeping a close eye on **Dillon Dingler**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** to ensure our bench depth remains prepared for potential mid-game defensive shifts.\n\nRegarding risk, managers should exercise caution with **Carson Benge** (51.46) as he faces the formidable Cole; while he holds a spot in our lineup, he is the most volatile asset today due to the SP skill delta. Conversely, **Trea Turner** (64.38) and **Colt Keith** (61.71) are locked in for production; **Colt Keith** specifically benefits from a strong platoon advantage against Gordon, making him an essential component of today\u2019s offensive strategy. We are proceeding with the current configuration as the optimal path to maximizing our 5x5 Roto output while balancing our hard game-cap constraints.",
